{
  "case_id": "2019-18-916",
  "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Thryv, Inc. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The text of the America Invents Act, the statutory history, the statute's policy goals, and this Court's decision in Cuozzo all confirm that Section 314(d) precludes judicial review of the director's time-barred determination under Section 315(b)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Cuozzo had a part that, of course, responded to concerns that have been raised, I -- I think in the dissent, and says we -- our interpretation does not enable the agency to act outside its statutory limits, for example; such shenanigans may be properly reviewable and focused really on the narrow issue before it. So how do we take into account that language from the decision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federal Respondent",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress established inter partes review as a quick and efficient means for the PTO to revisit issued patents and to cancel unpatentable claims. It proceeds in two steps, institution and trial. To prevent duplicative proceedings between the agency and the courts, Congress established a series of prerequisites to the institution of such a trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: -- I think you have a -- a -- a strong argument under Cuozzo. But what do you do with the language that Justice Ginsburg read from SAS and how would you reconcile SAS with your position here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ellis",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ELLIS: So I think, as far as reconciling the decision itself, I agree with my colleague that it just wasn't at issue in that case. The -- the limit on the Board's authority in that case was 318(a), the provision that -- that dictates the -- the contents of the final written decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ellis",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ELLIS: So I do think that this is a closely related decision. As we've discussed, it only speaks to institution. And if you have doubts --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, how about -- how about -- under this section, yes. How about that? How about the fact that, traditionally, executive branch agencies have considerable discretion in evaluating the merits of claims in deciding whether to proceed with enforcement actions, and, traditionally, statutes of limitations or repose were deadlines that are clear and written in law, tend to afford enforceable judicial rights to citizens?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ellis",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ELLIS: So, as I -- as I mentioned before, this is not a statute of repose. This Petitioner could challenge in the courts. This Petitioner could -- could join another IPR that was already proceeding. The director could institute review on the behalf of any other person."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ellis",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ELLIS: I don't think it's ambiguous, no. I think if there was any ambiguity in this provision, it was the one that was addressed in Cuozzo, whether it only applies for interlocutory appeals or after final written decisions. The Court decided that -- that question in Cuozzo, no one is asking to revisit it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But maybe one way to read Cuozzo -- and I take this to be the point of Justice Breyer's question -- is that it -- it goes beyond 314 but that it only goes to questions that are closely related to the reasonable likelihood determination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0001-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, it does, but you don't contest, right, that one -- if this Petitioner is thrown out, somebody else can bring another petition, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0001-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, Congress also said that there's no judicial review of the decision whether to institute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But, if you're right, Mr. Geyser, what does this unappealability bar really amount to? When does it bar anything that anybody would want to raise as an argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amici",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "amici on our side, you can see why they thought that the 315 bar is a fundamental safeguard to protect patent owners from both harassment and abuse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Spell that out. Spell that out. Why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But, if it's not with this Petitioner, it can be another petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-916",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "22fecc6f161e8f680c323699dee16fbf728198b16ac23448838fa30092d3d56f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22fecc6f161e-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
